  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Power to the Youth: Socially and economically empowered youth, along with CSOs, serve as change agents in five districts to meet developmental and governance challenges arising due to the spread COVID-19.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The action aims to empower low-income youth, socially and economically as change agents in their respective communities. The main objectives are: 1)  Local level public entities are engaging youth and providing support to GBV survivors; 2) Youth, especially low income vulnerable ones (women, PWDs, minorities) adversely affected by COVID19 are economically empowered; 3) CSOs and public institutions are actively tackling socio-environmental issues.</narrative>
  </description>
